Feral pigeons are of considerable epidemiological importance, being reservoirs and potential
vectors of a large number of microorganisms and source of antigens of zoonotic concern,
causing both infections and allergic diseases, that can be lethal (Haag-Wackernagel, 2006;
Haag-Wackernagel & Bircher, 2009; Haag-Wackernagel & Moch, 2004; Magnino et al., 2009;
Rosický, 1978).

